{
  "name": "2. SISS Funding Drip",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. SISS Funding Drip\n\nPilot only. Releases ONE curated funding lead per day into the JOB's tab so the dashboard has a steady feed.\n\n**Flow**\nDaily 08:00 -> read Funding_Signal -> pick oldest row where addedToJobs is false -> map to JOB's columns -> append to JOB's -> flip addedToJobs to TRUE.\n\n**Queue order** is oldest postedAt first, so June rounds go out before August ones and nothing sits until it is stale.\n\n**If the queue is empty** Pick One Signal returns zero items and the run ends quietly. No error, no empty row.\n\n**Two column facts this depends on**\n1. The JOB's header is `LeadStatus ` WITH A TRAILING SPACE. Map Funding to JOBs writes that exact key. Do not tidy it unless you also fix the sheet.\n2. JOB's has no companyIndustry, currency, roundFlavor or signalConfidence column. Those four are folded into leadNotes rather than dropped.\n\n**jobOpeningTitle** has no funding equivalent, so it is synthesized, e.g. `Series C funding, Quality build`.\n**jobDescription** is set to whySignalMatters, which is the funding rationale the dashboard renders as context.\n\nThis workflow only reads Funding_Signal and appends to JOB's. It never touches the job chain in workflow 1.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "fd-note",
      "name": "What This Does",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -160,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "1_KI5rgF7pweS-veuvKJ-Xt0E9VgrTtLHbuPBs1bfYOs",
          "mode": "id"
        },
